report+=['## Frozen protocol and evidence boundaries','','- Reuse saved map-enabled production artifacts at pinned commits; do not rebuild or tune settings after seeing outcomes. Verify every input bundle and map against the dataset manifest. The map-enabled build is the evaluated artifact population, not a byte-identical claim about a separately saved original build.','- Select loaded packages before reading recovery outcomes: rank deduplicated embedded JS-family source bytes, select all if fewer than ten, otherwise the ten largest. Include transitive packages. Exclude framework runtimes (`vue`, `vue-router`, `vuex`, `vue-server-renderer`, `react`, `react-dom`, `react-router`, `react-router-dom`, `scheduler`, `@vue/*`, `@angular/*`) and `*-loader` runtimes. Full rankings and omissions are saved per repository in `selection.json`.','- Keep exact source text and content hashes; normalize webpack namespaces, legacy `/~/` paths, and loader query suffixes for source resource identity. Differing source contents stay separate. No source/bundle function correspondences are provided to the graph extractor.','- Use the previous oracle policy unchanged: innermost own-body interior mapping points, at least two votes, at least 80% purity, and a strict unique winner. Unresolved functions remain recorded and are excluded from the supported-target denominator; library-origin unresolved counts and source-reference counts are included in the CSV. All selected source files parsed successfully in these runs.','- Keep the current per-chunk recovery boundary, radius one, sibling window two, undirected function relationships, 18,000-character size eligibility, synchronous rounds, and one-to-one source identity within a chunk. Anchors do not transfer across chunks. Extracted cross-chunk calls are recorded but do not expand this boundary.','- Recompute the original unique >=10-property-operation POG seed proposals over all selected references and each whole target-containing chunk. Because this is an oracle connectivity test, accept only oracle-confirmed original seed proposals. Record incorrect/unassessed proposals instead of letting wrong starting correspondences contaminate propagation.','- At every round select the exact oracle counterpart anywhere in the eligible neighborhood. No top-five cutoff, embeddings, model calls, or model-cache verdicts. Stop after an empty round. Unsupported or non-one-to-one oracle identities are not promoted as arbitrary bridge functions; any such supported cases remain in denominators with an explicit terminal gate.','- Compare baseline function graphs with the same graphs augmented by resolved calls from the frozen extractor. Do not repair legacy JSONP, array tables, Vite, ESM imports, custom runtimes, or other unsupported formats during this benchmark.','- No initialization-specific matching or module-membership expansion is added. Existing supported-function denominators remain intact; functions are not guessed to be initialization-only and removed.','', 'The extractor is an exact snapshot of `scripts/real-app/module-graph/build.mjs`, saved as `scripts/real-app/robustness/frozen-module-graph.mjs`. Snapshot hash: `'+sha(ROOT/'scripts/real-app/robustness/frozen-module-graph.mjs')+'`.','','Raw POG seed audits:','']
