report+=['','Two incorrect POG proposals occur in the webpack 5 subject. The results are therefore clean-seed connectivity bounds, not end-to-end accuracy with the unfiltered seed detector. Module-format non-recognition is reported separately from successful parsing; zero extracted modules does not count as successful module reconstruction.','','## Findings and next experiments','','1. The frozen module extractor is not bundler-independent: it recognizes the tested webpack 4/5 forms but not the tested webpack 1/3 or Vite forms. This confirms the portability concern.','2. Aggregate connectivity hides weak libraries. Consult the per-library table and macro averages; several small libraries have zero reachable targets despite high repository totals.','3. In the webpack 5 subject, the entire augmentation gain is in core-js (281 → 846 of 960); large prebundled libraries and UI packages do not automatically benefit.','4. Keep these results as the frozen baseline before adding adapters for legacy JSONP/array tables and ESM import/export links. Evaluate those changes as new ablations, without changing the pinned app builds or denominators.','5. A controlled causal robustness experiment should additionally bundle the same application/library inputs under multiple settings. This cross-repository study measures practical coverage, with library composition, source distribution, minification, and code splitting also varying.','','## Reproduce and inspect','','From `/Users/aaronxyliu/GitHub/FAPI Study`, run repositories in the order in `experiments/real-app/robustness/subjects.json`:','','```sh','node --max-old-space-size=8192 scripts/real-app/robustness/prepare.mjs <slug>','node --max-old-space-size=8192 scripts/real-app/robustness/run.mjs <slug>','python3 scripts/real-app/robustness/report.py','```','','Each subject folder contains `selection.json`, `prepared.json`, exact saved inputs, `detector-input.json`, `ground-truth.json`, `module-analysis.json`, `seed-audit.json`, `summary.json`, `target-traces.json`, and `repository-evidence.json`. The overview directory contains `library-rates.csv`, `summary.json`, and `verification.json`. All summaries include explicit denominators; rates are oracle connectivity rates, not LLM recovery or precision.','']
